    "turn_text": "no doubt about it. It's really a testament to the legacy of bourbon, what bourbon is contributed to the fabric of our country, the economic vitality, and so forth. So, Congressman, you know, the country's been grappling with a lot over the last three months. It's just really hard to take it all in. Certainly over the last two or three weeks with the George Floyd killing and so forth. And in Louisville in particular has had its own challenges. And I know Mayor Fisher and you've been in the middle of that with the sad death of Breona Taylor as well. We're all anxious to help address the long term. inequity with our African-American brothers and sisters. I have some hope that things can come together and Republicans and Democrats can come together, certainly working with the important role that law enforcement plays, but also warning from the events of the last four weeks in really bringing the country together.",
