    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, I am optimistic. And I think the protests we've seen, not just in Louisville and Kentucky, but across the country, but across the world, which are very, very diverse and very young is promising. And they're about so much more than police treatment of black citizens. Clearly, that's a huge problem and one which is a continuing shame for this country because it is from the legacy of slavery and white supremacy. And we have to deal with that. And Chris Hughes said, and I think the most important thing that you said, what can we do? And the importance of that is that government certainly has a role here. Government has a role in policy, particularly with regard to policing. But it's not just government. It cannot be just government. It has to be corporate America. It has to be the non-profit sector. It has to be the education system. We all have to focus on that very, very intently and intentionally.",
