    "turn_text": "I had the opportunity about four years ago. Just this discussion prompted my memory of it, of spending a couple of hours with Congressman John Lewis over at his office. And, you know, he's been on the front lines of us. for years and was severely beaten crossing the bridge and he told me he reflected on great stories about Martin Luther King and just about the overall struggle and I know John Lewis he's grappling through an illness right now as well but he is he is really the testament of of a leadership and, you know, the distilled spirits industry has a role to play in this as well. Just recently, there's been news that's come out for Jack Daniels, one of the gentlemen that helped create Jack Daniels and come up. with that recipe was an African-American gentleman. And there's a new distillery in Tennessee. Now that's in Tennessee, but our industry is committed to doing our part as well. So Congressman, the distilled spirits industry in Bourbon have enjoyed a lot of great success in 2007, 2008. That was in the early days of really Bourbon, really rise into the forefront. Could you just tell us what the growth of bourbon is meant to Kentucky and Louisville for sure. You go back 10 years and just how Louisville and in itself has changed dramatically in bringing bourbon to the forefront. It is really the signature product, that in the horse racer. for Kentucky. Could you tell us how in Kentucky, the bluegrass state has enjoyed the growth of bourbon over the last 10 to 15 years?",
